## Context

Measured 2026-11-12 by replaying the archived seat answers (agent-sessions
raw store, seat-raw, 426 files since 2026-10-31) through `gaze_seat.derive`:
all 20 seats refused for their reach line carried a valid
`reach: read=… shell=… tests=…` line. Each had progress text before the
header: one line ("Status: I've read the diff…", "Now let me write the
report:") on 17 Claude seats and 1 Vibe seat; a long tool trace on 2 Vibe
seats. Claude-family seats lost about 9% (17/194), still on 2026-11-12;
GPT 0/218. In the review notes of 15 repos since 2026-10-27, reach-line
refusals are 32 of 87 failed seats, the largest cause.

`reach_refusal` reads the reach line at the report's second line only
(ticket 1290, commit 22f3c16a3, against picking a reach line out of the
body). Ticket 1400 later refused any second valid reach line, which covers
the quoted-line risk on its own.

## Ask

Accept a short progress preamble: drop up to three leading non-blank lines
when the header (seat `worker:` line, `reach:` line, or a fenced header
block) follows them. A reach line deeper in the body stays refused.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A report with up to three lines of progress text before its header is filed, the preamble not in the filed report
- [ ] A reach line after more than three lines of body is still `no valid reach line`
- [ ] Replaying the 20 archived refusals: every one with a preamble of three lines or fewer is filed
- [ ] panel.md states the rule
